# The Dockerfile does `COPY . /var/www/html/`, so the build context IS the public
# webroot. Anything not excluded here is downloadable from slapbabydesigns.co.za.
# .gitignore does NOT apply to Docker builds — this file is the only control.

# --- Version control and tooling: a served .git/ hands over the whole source ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude
.dockerignore
Dockerfile

# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*

# --- CI-only helpers: smoke tests and the manifest check never run in the image -
scripts/

# --- Rebuilt inside the image (composer install runs after COPY) ---------------
vendor/
node_modules/

# --- Docs, design sources and archives ------------------------------------------
*.md
*.zip
# Claude Design canvases. assets/SLAP Logo.dc.html is the source the brand mark
# was drawn from; it sits under assets/, so without this line it would be served
# at /assets/SLAP%20Logo.dc.html — a sketch of the logo, on the live site, asking
# for a support.js that does not exist. The **/ is load-bearing and not noise:
# a bare *.dc.html would match the context root only, and the file is one
# directory down.
**/*.dc.html

# --- Local design material, not site content -----------------------------------
# The .dc.html design canvas, its 69KB support.js and the loose WhatsApp photos
# are the sisters' reference material. They are the source the site was drawn
# from, not the site — and the raw photos are far larger than the versions in
# assets/img/bears/.
SLAP Baby Designs website/
SLAP Baby Designs website.zip
WhatsApp Image*.jpeg
slap-baby-designs.css

# --- Runtime state -------------------------------------------------------------
/data/
*.log

# TRAP 1: docker/ must NOT be excluded. .dockerignore removes paths from the
# build context for EVERY COPY, including the two that place php-prod.ini and
# apache-security.conf — excluding it fails the build with "file not found".
# It reaches the webroot via `COPY . .`, so the Dockerfile deletes it after.
#
# TRAP 2: composer.json and composer.lock must NOT be excluded. The image runs
# `composer install` during build; without them PHPMailer is missing and every
# enquiry is saved but never emailed — a silent failure, not a loud one.
